						<h3>Parakeets are small birds native to Australia. They are characterized by long tails, zygodactyl feet (meaning they have 4 toes), and various color mutations. Most wild parakeets are bright green or yellow, but other colors such as blue, white, yellow, and violet have developed through captive breeding.</h3>
